Fixed. The bug was in `src/import_merge.ts:7` — the duplicate check compared URLs with a raw string match (`b.url === inc.url`), so `"https://EXAMPLE.com/a"` never matched `"https://example.com/a"`.

The fix reuses the repo's existing canonicalizer: a `urlKey()` helper that runs `normalizeUrl()` from `src/url_utils.ts` (it lowercases the hostname, strips tracking params, drops the bare trailing slash), with a fallback to the raw string if `new URL()` throws on a malformed bookmark. The match in `mergeImports` now compares canonical keys on both sides, so the case-insensitive duplicate is merged into the existing entry (tags unioned, no second entry, inputs not mutated). I intentionally didn't touch the semantics of `normalizeUrl` itself — its tracking-param behavior is out of scope for this bug.

Also added `tests/import_merge.test.ts` with three cases: hostname-case duplicate gets merged with tag union, non-matching URL appended unchanged, and no tag duplication / no input mutation.

Verified: `deno test` → 6 passed, 0 failed (3 new + 3 pre-existing); `deno check` on the touched files is clean. (The write-tool tsc linter flags TS5097/TS2304, but that's pre-existing noise — it runs without Deno's compiler flags, same as the other test files in this repo.)


